WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.060
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.600
And we're best friends.
而且我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.420
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你打造了这个名为“终极办公室重温”的播客节目。

6
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:19.400
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能讲述的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是办公室女士。

8
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.000
Guys, what's going on?
伙计们，怎么回事？

9
00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:26.860
How are ya?
你们好吗？

10
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.380
Wow, Angela, you're bringing the energy today.
哇，安吉拉，你今天活力十足啊。

11
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:31.160
I just played an hour of tennis.
我刚打了一个小时网球。

12
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:32.960
So you're amped up.
难怪你这么亢奋。

13
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:34.400
I'm like, someone throw a ball at me.
我感觉就像，谁来朝我扔个球吧。

14
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:35.080
I'm gonna hit it.
我要把它击飞。

15
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:36.280
I'm gonna do something with it.
我要用它做点什么。

16
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.180
But she's in her tennis uniform.
不过她穿着网球服呢。

17
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.660
So she really is ready.
所以她是真的很准备好了。

18
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:40.800
She's a uniform.
她穿着制服。

19
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:41.780
What is it?
那叫什么？

20
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:42.660
Tennis clothes?
网球服？

21
00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:43.260
Outfit.
行头。

22
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:47.180
I mean, you know, I'm not on a team.
我是说，你知道的，我没加入什么球队。

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.220
No, I guess that's true.
好吧，我想也是。

24
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:49.860
That's true.
确实。

25
00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:51.320
I would wear a tennis uniform.
我会愿意穿网球服的。

26
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.940
I mean, sign me up.
我是说，算我一个。

27
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.640
Did you notice that all the men during the U.S.
你有没有注意到美国网球公开赛期间

28
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.960
Open were wearing kind of the same tennis shirt?
所有男球员穿的网球衫都差不多？

29
00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.800
It was like a gray, burgundy thing.
有点像灰色搭酒红色的款式。

30
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:02.720
There was lots of burgundy and pink.
有很多酒红色和粉色。

31
00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:03.280
Yeah.
对啊。

32
00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.680
And kind of a modern neckline.
还有那种很现代的领口。

33
00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:07.560
It reminded me of the shirts from Star Trek.
让我想起了《星际迷航》里的衣服。

34
00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:08.320
Yeah.
对。

35
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.860
It felt very Trekkie to me.
我觉得非常有星际迷航的感觉。

36
00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:10.560
Very Trekkie.
非常有星际迷航风。

37
00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.900
Look at you with a sci-fi reference.
瞧瞧你，都会用科幻梗了。

38
00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:13.800
I know.
我知道。

39
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:14.640
And tennis.
还有网球。

40
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:15.020
What's happening?
这是怎么了？

41
00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.000
Am I becoming you?
我是在变成你吗？

42
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.440
Am I gonna come in a tennis outfit next week?
我下周也会穿着网球装来吗？

43
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.640
Oh, I hope so.
哦，我希望如此。

44
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:21.300
Maybe.
也许吧。

45
00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:25.220
Well, today we are talking about Viewing Party.
好了，我们今天要聊的是《观影派对》。

46
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.500
It is Season 7, Episode 8, written by John Vitti and directed by Ken Whittingham.
这是第七季第八集，由约翰·维蒂编剧，肯·惠廷汉姆执导。

47
00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.420
New writer alert, John Vitti.
新编剧警报，约翰·维蒂。

48
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:41.220
He came to us after writing for The Simpsons and King of the Hill and was nominated for an Emmy Award for writing episodes of The Larry Sanders Show.
他曾在为《辛普森一家》和《山丘之王》编剧后加入我们，并因编剧《拉里·桑德斯秀》而获得艾美奖提名。

49
00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.380
And he also wrote The Angry Birds Movie, which is a favorite of my kids.
他还写了《愤怒的小鸟大电影》，那是我孩子们最喜欢的电影之一。

50
00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:46.880
My kids love that movie.
我的孩子们超喜欢那部电影。

51
00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:47.340
Yeah.
对。

52
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.280
I love it too.
我也很喜欢。

53
00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:51.300
He was new for this season and he wrote Viewing Party.
他这季刚加入，写了《观影派对》那一集。

54
00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.640
Would you like a summary?
你想听剧情概要吗？

55
00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.100
So much.
非常喜欢。

56
00:01:54.460 --> 00:01:54.760
Okay.
好。

57
00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:02.100
Aaron and Gabe host a glee viewing party, but Michael's hatred toward Gabe threatens to ruin the evening.
亚伦和盖比举办了一场《欢乐合唱团》观影派对，但迈克尔对盖比的厌恶险些毁了整个晚上。

58
00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.540
He is in such poor form.
他的状态太差了。

59
00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.740
Michael is like a little kid.
迈克尔就像个小孩子。

60
00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:12.920
Andy has an adverse reaction after ingesting wine and crushed seahorses.
安迪在喝下葡萄酒和海马粉后产生了不良反应。

61
00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:20.760
Meanwhile, Jim and Pam are conflicted to discover that the key to soothing a crying Cece is Dwight.
与此同时，吉姆和帕姆惊讶地发现，能哄住大哭的西西的关键人物竟然是德怀特，这让他们很纠结。

62
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.860
Yeah, and they're gonna interrupt part of the punch card action.
对，而且他们会打断一部分打卡环节。

63
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:26.480
Yes, I was gonna say.
对，我正想说这个。

64
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:31.020
Angela spends a large portion of the evening nudie in a car.
安吉拉在车里度过了大半个晚上的裸体镜头。

65
00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:32.280
Fake nudie.
假裸。

66
00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.580
I was gonna ask you what you really had on when we get there.
我本来打算等我们到了之后问你里面到底穿了什么。

67
00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.340
Well, fast fact number one was a fan question from Sarah M.
好，趣味冷知识第一条来自宾夕法尼亚州哈里斯堡的萨拉·M的粉丝提问。

68
00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.500
in Harrisburg, Pennsylvania.
宾夕法尼亚州哈里斯堡。

69
00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.620
Why did they pick Glee as the show to watch for the viewing party?
为什么他们会选择《欢乐合唱团》作为观影派对观看的节目？

70
00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.480
I'm curious about that too.
我也很好奇这一点。

71
00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.300
Do you know the answer?
你知道答案吗？

72
00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:54.080
Well, at the time, Glee was, I believe it was, the highest rated scripted show of any network.
嗯，当时《欢乐合唱团》是，我相信它是所有电视台收视率最高的电视剧。

73
00:02:54.580 --> 00:03:01.800
And supposedly at the 2010 Emmy Awards, the office producers and writers were seated near the folks from Glee.
据说在2010年艾美奖上，《办公室》的制片人和编剧们的座位挨着《欢乐合唱团》剧组的人。

74
00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:11.280
And Paul Lieberstein told me that during the commercial breaks, he started chatting up one of the showrunners from Glee, Brad Falchick.
保罗·利伯斯坦告诉我，在广告期间，他开始和《欢乐合唱团》的一位剧集运作人布拉德·法尔查克闲聊。

75
00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:15.580
And Paul pitched this idea to him at the Emmy Awards.
然后保罗在艾美奖上把这个想法推销给了他。

76
00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:19.380
This idea of the folks from the office having a Glee viewing party.
就是《办公室》里的人举办一场《欢乐合唱团》观影派对这个想法。

77
00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.560
And Brad liked it?
然后布拉德喜欢吗？

78
00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.360
He loved it.
他非常喜欢。

79
00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:22.680
He said, I give my blessing.
他说，我批准了。

80
00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:23.680
Amazing.
太棒了。

81
00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.760
Well, it wasn't that easy.
好吧，其实没那么简单。

82
00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.980
Because, you know, Glee was on Fox.
因为你知道，《欢乐合唱团》在福克斯播出。

83
00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.200
It was on NBC.
而我们在全国广播公司。

84
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:30.720
The suits got involved.
高层们介入了。

85
00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:31.360
They did.
确实如此。

86
00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:36.400
Randy had a lot to say about how difficult it was to pull this off.
兰迪对促成这件事有多艰难发表了很多看法。

87
00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:38.340
I bet they're a bunch of fun stoppers.
我敢打赌他们是一群扫兴鬼。

88
00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:39.400
Yeah.
对。

89
00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.660
We had a couple of fan questions.
我们还有几个粉丝提问。

90
00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:49.560
Natalie V from Winnipeg asked, is there a process for asking one network to shoot an episode that promotes another network?
来自温尼伯的娜塔莉·V问：向一个电视台申请拍摄一集宣传另一个电视台的剧集有什么流程吗？

91
00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:57.980
And Leah Roberts from Downington, Pennsylvania said, did you have to get special rights to use the Glee content in your episode?
宾夕法尼亚州唐宁敦的莉亚·罗伯茨说：你们在这一集中使用《欢乐合唱团》的内容需要获得特殊版权吗？

92
00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.800
I'd love to know the story behind all of this.
我很想知道这一切背后的故事。

93
00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:09.440
Well, Randy told us that the folks at Fox approved this episode, but they really pulled back on the amount of footage we could use.
嗯，兰迪告诉我们，福克斯的人批准了这一集，但他们对我们能使用的素材量进行了严格限制。

94
00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:12.840
We couldn't run any unaired clips from Glee.
我们不能播放任何《欢乐合唱团》未播出的片段。

95
00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:16.420
We could only use clips from older shows that had already aired.
我们只能使用已经播出的老剧集的片段。

96
00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:22.220
But that kind of went against our idea that we had all gathered to watch this brand new episode.
但这有点违背了我们“大家聚在一起看这集全新剧集”的设定。

97
00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:25.940
So we had to kind of like, you know.
所以我们不得不，你知道的。

98
00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:28.260
Scoochy, scoochy around it.
巧妙地、变通地绕过这个限制。

99
00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:29.420
Kind of make it work.
设法搞定它。

100
00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.380
Like, if you notice, there's very few clips.
比如，如果你注意的话，里面其实只有非常少的片段。

101
00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:35.540
That's also because it was very expensive.
这也是因为成本非常高。

102
00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:41.020
They had to pay large fees to any performer, writer, or director credited in the clip.
他们必须向片段中署名的任何演员、编剧或导演支付巨额费用。

103
00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.960
Remember, that's what happened with The Banker.
记住，这就是《银行家》那一集发生的事。

104
00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:45.060
It ended up being a really expensive episode.
结果那一集变得成本极高。

105
00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.160
They also had to pay any music licensing fees.
他们还得支付任何音乐版权费用。

106
00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.400
So Randy said we managed to go ahead with it.
所以兰迪说我们还是设法推进了。

107
00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:57.120
And what we did was, if you notice, a lot of times our characters are describing what they're seeing.
我们的做法是，如果你注意的话，很多时候我们的角色都在描述他们看到的东西。

108
00:04:57.320 --> 00:05:01.100
And you just see like a flash of a Glee character on the screen.
屏幕上你只会看到《欢乐合唱团》角色的一个闪回镜头。

109
00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:05.280
But you don't really gather any plot from the actual clips.
但你实际上无法从那些真实片段中获取任何剧情。

110
00:05:05.940 --> 00:05:07.200
So that's how we did it.
所以我们就是这么做的。

111
00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.020
Well, I think it was short-sighted on the suits.
嗯，我觉得那些高层真是目光短浅。

112
00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:10.760
I do.
我是这么觉得。

113
00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:11.360
Yeah.
对。

114
00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:12.080
Because guess what?
因为你猜怎么着？

115
00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:15.540
Had they put some of their clips in our show, it would have been such a huge buzz.
要是他们把一些片段放到我们的剧里，那会引起多大的轰动啊。

116
00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.120
It would have driven more people to Glee.
那会吸引更多人去看《欢乐合唱团》。

117
00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:20.800
I don't think they needed more people to be driven to Glee is their point.
他们的观点是，他们觉得不需要吸引更多人来看《欢乐合唱团》。

118
00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:23.900
They're like, we already have a larger viewing audience than you.
他们的态度就像是，我们的观众群体本来就比你们大。

119
00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:26.140
They're like, we don't need you guys.
他们就好像在说，我们不需要你们。

120
00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.500
They're like, here's a few puny clips.
他们的态度就像是，给你们这几个微不足道的片段。

121
00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:28.980
You're welcome.
不用谢。

122
00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:29.320
Yeah.
对。

123
00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.600
It's like my friend, her honeymoon was in Hawaii.
这就好比我的朋友，她的蜜月是在夏威夷度过的。

124
00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:34.700
And she kept thinking she'd get free stuff if she said she was on her honeymoon.
她一直以为只要说自己在度蜜月就能拿到免费的东西。

125
00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.060
And they were literally like, take a number.
结果他们真的就像是说，请排队拿号吧。

126
00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:37.580
Yeah.
对。

127
00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:39.760
You and everyone else.
你和所有人一样。

128
00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:41.880
All right.
好吧。

129
00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.720
Are you ready for fast fact number two?
准备好听第二个快速冷知识了吗？

130
00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:44.220
Yeah.
好。

131
00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.720
This is a fan question from Faye B.
这是来自新罕布什尔州的Faye B.提出的粉丝问题。

132
00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:47.660
in New Hampshire.
新罕布什尔州的。

133
00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.960
Was this episode filmed at someone's apartment?
这一集是在某个人的公寓里拍摄的吗？

134
00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.640
And if so, whose was it?
如果是的话，是谁的？

135
00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:54.460
Well, Faye, it was not.
嗯，费伊，并不是。

136
00:05:54.980 --> 00:06:01.400
This entire interior location, Gabe's apartment, was built by our crew,
这个完整的内部取景地——盖布的公寓，是由我们的剧组搭建的，

137
00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:05.860
designed by Michael Gallenberg, built by our construction head, Tim James,
由迈克尔·加伦伯格设计，我们的施工负责人蒂姆·詹姆斯建造，

138
00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:10.260
and then decorated by our set decorating team, headed by Steve Rothstein.
然后由史蒂夫·罗斯斯坦领导的布景团队进行装饰。

139
00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:12.180
I mean, what a phenomenal job.
我是说，这工作做得太棒了。

140
00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:12.720
I know.
我知道。

141
00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.300
It is so well done.
真的做得太好了。

142
00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:18.920
We're going to get to this in later seasons, but I felt the same way in Oscar's apartment.
我们后面的季度会聊到这个，但我对奥斯卡公寓的感觉也是一样的。

143
00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.040
They built the whole thing.
他们把整个都搭建出来了。

144
00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.680
Well, I guess this was a really big endeavor because they had to build multiple connecting
嗯，我想这是一个非常大的工程，因为他们不仅要建造多个相连的房间，还要在厨房里建造带有吊扇的跌落式吊顶。

145
00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:28.740
rooms as well as a drop ceiling with a ceiling fan in the kitchen.
对。

146
00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:29.260
Yeah.
因为你知道，当迈克尔抛披萨面团时，剧本里写的就是它会砸到风扇上。

147
00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:34.020
Because, you know, when Michael tosses the pizza dough, that was scripted that it would hit the fan.
所以他们必须好好把这个设计出来。

148
